      "answer": "Yes",
      "reason_rejected": "This position relies on an anachronistic interpretation that 'fair' simply means 'according to the custom of the time.' While exchanges were customary, the structural coercion and lack of voluntary agency inherent in serfdom mean they do not meet the standard criteria for 'fair trade' (equity and voluntary exchange). Even if terms were 'customary,' the inability to exit the relationship negates the 'trade' aspect of voluntary exchange."
